AmiDT - fast, small picture datatypes
=====================================

Datatypes let MultiView, AmiFM's View and every other datatypes program
show pictures. AmiDT's are written to be quick on a plain 68020/68030 and to
keep memory use low.

New formats (nothing on the system is replaced):
  Targa (TGA)   colour-mapped, true colour, grey; plain or RLE; any origin
  PCX           mono, 16 colours (EGA), 4-bit, 256 colours, 24-bit
  ICO           Windows icons (the biggest picture in the icon; BMP or PNG inside)
  QOI           "Quite OK Image" pictures

Faster PNG, GIF and BMP (optional - replaces the system's classes):
  They make the picture with up to 256 colours themselves (true colour is
  dithered), so the system does not have to convert it afterwards. On an
  A1200 with a 68030 at 50 MHz, a 640x480 picture:

                      AmiDT            AmigaOS 3.2
    PNG true colour   5.3 s,   32 KB   17.5 s, 1207 KB
    PNG 256 colours   1.8 s            3.7 s
    BMP true colour   1.5 s,   30 KB   12.0 s, 1213 KB
    GIF 256 colours   3.0 s            4.7 s

  On a graphics card (RTG) screen the system's PNG datatype can show true
  colour in full. When Picasso96 or CyberGraphX is installed, the installer
  asks whether you view pictures on the graphics card; if so it keeps the
  system's own PNG, GIF and BMP datatypes (AmiDT's are only added where the
  system has none).

Needs AmigaOS 3.0 or newer and a 68020 or better.

Installing
  Double-click Install_AmiDT. The system's own PNG, GIF and BMP datatypes are
  kept in SYS:Classes/DataTypes/AmiDT-Originals; run the installer again and
  pick Remove to put them back.

JPEG
  AmiDT has no JPEG datatype: JFIFdt44 (Aminet gfx/show/JFIFdt44.lha) is the
  fast one. Install it, then run Install_AmiDT again and it sets JFIFdt44 to
  its fast 256-colour mode (ENVARC:classes/datatypes/jfif44.prefs =
  "V42MODE DITHER=ORDERED"): 4.7 s instead of 14.4 s for a 640x480 JPEG.
